[b]Shroudweave Minimap 0.5.16[/b]

A client-side minimap with the HD map, live fog of war, player and location markers, and a weather clock. No server mod needed. Round north-up stays the default, and Creative Mode 3.0.0 guards remain in place.

[b]What's new in 0.5.16[/b]
[list]
[*]Optional square map with a matching gold frame and corrected square terrain rendering.
[*]Glow for players, pings and waypoints, with same-colour or contrasting styles. All glow is on by default. Death markers get a dark backplate and red rim.
[*]Top-right is the default for new configurations. Existing configured positions are kept.
[*]Renderer startup and frame-upload fixes to address missing rendering/borders.
[*]GPU terrain and icon drawing, cached clock/weather geometry, and less repeated background work.
[/list]
The performance changes may help. Hopefully they improve your FPS, but a gain is not guaranteed. Not every reported border issue is confirmed resolved either.

[b]Installation[/b]
1. Close Enshrouded. Back up mods/minimap_mod outside the mods folder and back up shroudtopia.json.
2. Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/216]Shroudtopia Shroudweave[/url] using its instructions. The loader has a separate listing because several mods use it, so everyone can use one shared download and update page.
3. Extract the complete Minimap 0.5.16 ZIP into the game folder, overwriting matching Minimap files. The DLL, images and shaders belong in mods/minimap_mod. This full release includes the required assets.
4. Keep your existing shroudtopia.json and other mods/settings. Edit the existing mods.minimap_mod section when changing options; don't add a duplicate section.

[b]Options[/b]
Round north-up, the HD map, sample step 2, top-right and offset 0 are the defaults. Existing configured values remain in effect.

map_shape: round or square. Square stays north-up; round also supports map_orientation: rotating.
position: top-right, middle-right, bottom-right, top-left, middle-left or bottom-left.
offset: positive moves up, negative moves down, relative to your chosen position. Scales with resolution and is clamped to the screen.

Square may need a small offset to avoid the Journal or other HUD elements. offset: -16 moved it down enough in one tested setup. Adjust it for your display; the default stays 0.

map_style: default uses the HD map, original uses the original texture.
icon_style: original keeps plain markers, world-map adds gold frames and brighter backplates. You can mix these independently. Check the Images tab for an impression of these settings.

player_arrow_glow, ping_glow, waypoint_glow and death_marker_glow can each be turned off. The first three have a matching _style setting: same-colour is the default, contrasting is the alternative. Death markers use the dark backplate with red rim.

[b]Controls[/b]
F10 or numpad *: show/hide. + and -: zoom. F9/F11: smaller/larger.
Keys are configurable below. Readable names such as F8, Insert, Delete, numpadplus and letters work, along with hexadecimal values. Use none to disable a binding.

[b]Default settings[/b]
Merge this section into your existing shroudtopia.json, beside Enshrouded.exe. Keep other mods' settings. If mods.minimap_mod already exists, edit it rather than adding it again.
[code]
{
  "mods": {
    "minimap_mod": {
      "active": true,
      "position": "top-right",
      "offset": 0,
      "map_shape": "round",
      "map_orientation": "north-up",
      "toggle_key": "F10",
      "render_camera_fallback": true,
      "debug_logging": false,
      "show_other_players": true,
      "show_pings": true,
      "show_waypoints": true,
      "show_world_markers": true,
      "show_death_markers": true,
      "map_light": 55,
      "map_style": "default",
      "icon_style": "original",
      "heading_smoothing_ms": 55,
      "player_arrow_glow": true,
      "player_arrow_glow_style": "same-colour",
      "ping_glow": true,
      "ping_glow_style": "same-colour",
      "waypoint_glow": true,
      "waypoint_glow_style": "same-colour",
      "death_marker_glow": true,
      "map_sample_step": 2,
      "max_icons": 64,
      "show_clock": true,
      "show_weather": true,
      "show_fog_of_war": true,
      "toggle_key_secondary": "0x6A",
      "zoom_in_key": "0xBB",
      "zoom_in_key_secondary": "0x6B",
      "zoom_out_key": "0xBD",
      "zoom_out_key_secondary": "0x6D",
      "scale_percent": 100,
      "size_decrease_key": "F9",
      "size_increase_key": "F11"
    }
  }
}
[/code]

[b]Still being worked on[/b]
Native map POI filters are not yet mirrored completely. Current-location/region labels and Hollow Halls interior maps are not included. Linux/Proton issues remain under investigation.

For missing maps or frames, please send the full shroudtopia.log from startup and a screenshot. For FPS reports, compare visible and hidden in the same spot after the toggle banner clears.

